### `src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/contracts.py`

Add four fields to `ChildEntryContractV1`, all defaulting to empty tuples:

- `nonstrict_document_reads: Tuple[Tuple[str, Literal["inherits", "drops", "fresh"]], ...]`
- `nonstrict_process_reads: Tuple[Tuple[str, bool], ...]`
- `process_property_writes: Tuple[str, ...]`
- `establishing_process_property_writes: Tuple[str, ...]`

The document-read fields are the bare DDP name and its relation to invocation-entry properties:

- `inherits`: an entry property reaches this read.
- `drops`: the child’s path discards an entry property before this read.
- `fresh`: a No Data boundary prevents the caller’s entry properties from reaching it.

The process-read fields are the bare DPP name and `local_later_leg_writer`. That boolean records an internal later-leg dependency and survives forwarding.

The two DPP writer sets contain:

- Every known authored or contracted DPP writer.
- The subset the execution-scope writer-existence rule counts, excluding unwaited calls transitively.

Document their existence-only meaning. Do not substitute `mutated_state` or `guaranteed_state`: the former disappears when effects are incomplete, and the latter omits conditional writers.

Keep `nonstrict_cached_reads` unchanged. Its cache-less row represents a retrieved/property-loss context; its caller application forces `CACHE_TRANSFER_UNPROVED` and therefore serves `PROCESS_IR_SEMANTIC_LINEAGE_PROPERTY_READ_BEFORE_WRITE`. That is incorrect for an untouched entry-document read with a sibling writer, whose code is `PROCESS_IR_SEMANTIC_LINEAGE_DDP_SCOPE_INVALID`. The deciding branches are [lineage.py:2312](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/lineage.py:2312) and [lineage.py:3195](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/lineage.py:3195).

