Do not mark X invalidated merely because a script was encountered. `_drop_replaced_document_keys` invalidates only keys actually carried and dropped. Consequently, a script between entry and read still yields SCOPE when X exists solely on sibling documents, but yields BEFORE when arriving X was discarded. [lineage.py:922](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/lineage.py:922)

Apply the new rows in `_discharge_child_contract`:

For a document row:

- `inherits`: discharge when the arriving caller documents establish X. Otherwise, if a writer exists, classify using the caller’s actual invalidation and retrieved-cache provenance.
- `drops`: arriving X cannot discharge the read. Add X to the classification’s invalidated set only if the arriving documents actually carried it. Preserve existing invalidation; never manufacture it from a sibling-only writer.
- `fresh`: discard caller document establishment, invalidation, and cache provenance for this judgment. A writer elsewhere produces SCOPE; no writer permits absence.
- When this process cannot fail the read, forward an observation at the call so its own contract carries the conditional obligation.
- A `fresh` cut remains fresh through further calls.

For a process row:

- Discharge if the caller’s execution state establishes P.
- Otherwise ask `_nonstrict_read_can_fail(prepared, (DPP, P), capabilities)`.
- With no establishing writer, tolerate absence and forward the row.
- With a writer, classify using the row’s internal later-leg flag OR the caller’s later-leg predicate.
- Forward the combined flag through intermediate callers that cannot discharge the read.

Use the call node’s existing diagnostic pointer for lineage errors, with subprocess evidence. Profile obligations continue using `/process_ref`.

Factor the DPP writer-existence collection so the exported facts and their consumers agree:

- `_established_anywhere` consumes the establishing writer set of waited derived calls.
- `_leg_write_index` consumes all known DPP writers to locate them, including conditional writers.
- The all-writes collector and export share the same authored/contracted writer collection.
- Unwaited calls contribute no execution-scoped establishing writer.
- Keep `_awaited_guarantee`, `_child_guarantee`, and actual state transfer unchanged.

This is required for the sibling sweep: the current indexes see only a derived child’s guaranteed writes, while a flattened graph counts its direct conditional DPP writers. [lineage.py:1462](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/lineage.py:1462), [lineage.py:4100](/Users/gleb/Documents/Projects/Renera/boomi-mcp-server/src/boomi_mcp/compiler/process_ir/semantic_validation/lineage.py:4100)

